// Round tf: three of four team runs waited inside the driver's synchronous timeout, which stalled every other request and overshot the limit.
const BOUNDED_WAIT = 'A wait the spec bounds (a locked store, a busy resource) never blocks the thread that answers other requests: give a synchronous driver a timeout of 0 and retry the refused step on a timer (the whole transaction when it had already read), with the values the request already took (its clock reading), until the limit on a monotonic clock, so other requests are answered meanwhile and the reply comes at the limit, not later; a request that only reads takes no write lock, and on a store with one write lock for the whole database (SQLite) a transaction that writes takes that lock as it begins (BEGIN IMMEDIATE, retried as above): a read lock upgraded later is refused at once while another connection writes, so its retries can miss every gap until the limit.'

